<title>HONG KONG: Nanyang 1996 profit rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Nanyang 1996 profit rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   507.0	vs  52.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    40.0	 vs  30.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  250.5 gain vs  1.0 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    253.3	vs  26.1</p>
<p>    Turnover		     261.1	vs  266.0</p>
<p>    Company name		 Nanyang Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 19-25</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   June 25</p>
<p>NOTE - Yarn and garment manufacturer Nanyang Holdings also engages in property investments.</p>
<p>The company proposed a cash bonus of HK$0.85 per share vs nil.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$144.9 million on disposal of investment properties, gain of HK$109.7 million on disposal of properties held for sale, gain of HK$4.5 million on disposal of fixed assets, loss of HK$7.1 million on severance and other related payments and loss of HK$1.5 million on disposal of stocks.</p>
<p>Total dividend for the year is 125 H.K. cents (including cash bonus) vs 30 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
